"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions, enhancing security, accessibility, and data visualization tools, potentially leveraging AI algorithms to increase efficiency by 20%. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with Marcus Cole as the leader, followed by a design phase led by Omar Jensen. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase, celebrated in October, and a budget adjustment to $550,000 to support real-time analytics integration. The project is currently in the development phase, with security protocols updated for multi-factor authentication and encryption effective next January. There are also ongoing discussions regarding a potential partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. Feedback on the prototype is being sought from stakeholders, with a deadline at the end of November."
